    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0335" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.51c39/289</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-18">May 18, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Gilson called to see me two days ago and in his conversation said that he
                    felt it was desirable not to suggest any change in the existing arrangement
                    between the Government of Salvador and the bondholders until after the next
                    Presidential elections had taken place. I said that, in general, I concurred in
                    his opinion, but stated that I did not wish to make any definite statement in
                    the matter until after receipt of the requested report from the American
                    Legation in San Salvador. I further said that I would let him know when the
                    report had been received and have a further conference with him.</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">elles</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
